statement:
Let $k$ be bounded on $[0,1]^2$ and continuous off finitely many continuous curves $x=\varphi_i(y)$ and $y=\psi_j(x)$. Let $A$ be the [absolutely continuous](c:absolutely-continuous-measure) [probability measures](c:probability-measure) on $[0,1]$ and $M$ all of them. Then $\sup_{\mu\in A}\inf_{
u\in M}k(\mu,
u)=\inf_{
u\in M}\sup_{\mu\in A}k(\mu,
u)$.
